# Flight-mode settings on top of the calibration operating point. Every flight, replay or
# live, sources them; UNSET all of these for calibration runs.
# deploy_vio.py puts a copy of this file into each flight folder and appends the lens terms of
# that calibration (OV_NONRADIAL) as its last line: fly with the folder's copy. Without that
# line the lens terms start at zero (or at an OV_NONRADIAL left in the shell), which is right
# only for a calibration made without them. The fisheye mask of point 5 is in the folder's
# estimator_flight.yaml.
#
# 1. Calibration-prior stiffness: x0.10 of the stock standard deviations. Read by the patched
#    State.cpp at startup (initial covariance of the online-calibration states).
OV_PRIOR_DT_SIG=0.001
OV_PRIOR_EXTR_Q_SIG=0.0005
OV_PRIOR_EXTR_T_SIG=0.0015
OV_PRIOR_INTR_F_SIG=0.1
OV_PRIOR_INTR_D_SIG=0.0005
# 2. ADDED 2026-10-09: the two lens terms per camera stay calibration states in flight, with
#    x0.10 of the 0.002 a calibration uses; the third term is held. Kannala-Brandt
#    (equidistant) cameras only: for another camera model unset these two variables.
OV_PRIOR_NONRAD_SIG=0.0002
OV_NONRAD_SKEW_FIXED=1
# 3. ADDED 2026-10-09: features are matched between neighbouring cameras
#    (ov_core/src/track/xcam_assoc.inc), with the flight preset: at most 30 features are
#    searched per set of images, and each match is checked by a search back. This runs where
#    the four images of an instant reach the tracker as one set: the live node
#    run_online_msckf, and a replay with OV_GROUP_CAMS=1 (campaign.env sets it on the
#    vehicle). Where the images arrive one camera at a time, the estimator prints one
#    [xcam-warn] line and does not match. (The same line can appear once in a healthy flight,
#    for an incomplete set of images; "[xcam-total] ... runs=N" at the end tells how many sets
#    were matched.) Measured in the live node: about 3 ms more per set of images, a better
#    camera geometry during the flight, and a higher tracking error on average
#    (vio/README.md). To fly without it, unset these two after sourcing this file.
OV_XCAM=1
OV_XCAM_PRESET=rt
# 4. ADDED 2026-10-14: four limits for slow flight. While the vehicle hovers or flies slowly,
#    nearly every feature stays tracked through the whole clone window and one filter update
#    takes them all: 2500-6300 measurement rows, 135-250 ms on the Orin NX against 33 ms
#    between two sets of images, and the node runs 0.3-0.5 s behind for as long as the vehicle
#    is slow (two shadow flights of nxt3, 13 Oct 2026). vio/README.md, "Slow flight", has what
#    was measured. Unset, each of them is off and the estimator is the one of before.
#      OV_MSCKF_MAX_OBS    of one feature, at most this many observations per camera go into
#                          an MSCKF update (spread evenly over its track)
#      OV_MSCKF_ROWS       rows of window-end features per clone tick, and per update together
#                          with the lost features; what does not fit waits for a later tick.
#                          Needs OV_MSCKF_MAX_OBS to keep up with a hover.
#      OV_SPREAD_ONE_GATE  one update gate for all cameras: a set of images that lacks a camera
#                          no longer leaves the cameras ticking at different instants for the
#                          rest of the flight (10-15 clone ticks per second instead of 7)
#      OV_ZUPT_MAX_DZ      metres: no zero-velocity update further than this above or below
#                          the height of the last one, so none while the vehicle hovers
OV_MSCKF_MAX_OBS=12
OV_MSCKF_ROWS=900
OV_SPREAD_ONE_GATE=1
OV_ZUPT_MAX_DZ=0.3
# 5. ADDED 2026-11-07: the bearing measurement model, as the calibration passes of selfcalib run
#    it: every observation is used as a unit direction computed from its raw pixel, so the ring
#    of the image beyond about 86 deg off the axis is measured instead of extrapolated; the
#    tracker keeps the shipped RANSAC within 80 deg. It flies only with the fisheye mask the
#    calibration fitted to each lens: deploy_vio.py writes the mask of the pass the calibration
#    published (report.json w_mask) into the flight folder's estimator_flight.yaml, as it was
#    fitted. A calibration made without the model (before 2026-11-07, or with --no-bearing), or
#    one whose fitted mask cannot fly as it is (deploy_vio.py says why, with a WARNING), is
#    deployed without it: that folder's copy of this file sets OV_KB_BEARING=0 instead. Do not
#    fly this file with the package's estimator_flight.yaml as it is: fly a deployed folder.
#    Measured on the Orin NX in real time, 11 flights x 3 runs with and without the model
#    (7 Nov 2026): the same tracking error (3.69 against 3.73 cm), about 10 % more time per set
#    of images, 1 ms more median delay (vio/README.md, "Bearing measurement model").
#    To fly the original model, deploy the calibration with OV_KB_BEARING=0 exported (or
#    deploy_vio.py --no-bearing): that folder flies the estimator of before byte for byte.
#    Exporting OV_KB_BEARING=0 after sourcing a folder deployed with the model switches the
#    model off but keeps its fitted mask, which is narrower: not the original flight.
#    Kannala-Brandt (equidistant) cameras only, like point 2.
OV_KB_BEARING=1
OV_BEARING_ALL=1
OV_BEARING_RANSAC=1
# An estimator built before commit 6bbaf8c has neither addition: it ignores OV_PRIOR_NONRAD_SIG,
# OV_NONRAD_SKEW_FIXED, OV_XCAM and OV_XCAM_PRESET, and OV_NONRADIAL as well. One built before
# the commit that added point 4 ignores its four variables, and one built before commit 250f9f2
# the three of point 5 (it then flies the original model with the fitted mask).
# Measured on the Orin NX: vio/README.md, "Matching and lens terms in flight".
